        "reason": "deploy",
        "commitMessage": "Restore compact origin-bound ladders and separate FINAL outlook from lock and value\n\nKeep five concise EARLY/SCALP rows and original direction, ASK, time and serial together. Move full qualification, economics, IDs, source explanations and issued history into collapsed disclosures. Maintain single display ownership and source-expiry behavior. FINAL shows model outlook, target relationship and market prices separately from unchanged 90% qualified-call policy and model-implied settlement value.\n\nReject the demonstrated SCALP 95.1c case because its configured +5c risk arm requires a BID above the contract payout. Use the existing policy arm, not an arbitrary price ceiling; preserve native momentum, costs, serial entries, reversals and defensive exits. Past movement and maximum payout remain observations/bounds, never expected profit. Explicitly retain unproven trade value instead of inventing a forecast or new unconditional entry veto.\n\nTransfer SCALP origin/history from current deployment 5171df0d-1134-4e1c-a338-f8a033b8a8f0. MAIN EARLY/FINAL strategy and frozen artifacts unchanged. Focused validation: 30 Python regressions and native-output DOM checks including 84.4% FINAL at 92c, 95.1c rejection, 94c and low-price eligibility, gaps, terminal exits, and stable rendering.",
        "commitHash": "6e04aced0f718b29f8ed805abcc0f76b01ed5096",
        "branch": "fix/btc15-clean-live-ladders-20261009"
      }
    },
